## Testing Checklist

### Connection Tests
- [ ] Test connection establishment (passive mode)
- [ ] Test connection reuse (multiple operations without reconnect)
- [ ] Test connection recovery after error
- [ ] Test connection cleanup on client destruction

### Operation Tests
- [ ] List files in root directory
- [ ] List files in subdirectory
- [ ] Download small file (< 1KB)
- [ ] Download large file (> 100KB)
- [ ] Upload small file
- [ ] Upload large file
- [ ] Delete file
- [ ] Get system files (ALARM.NC, POSNI1.NC, MONTR.NC)
- [ ] Get programs list with O-number filtering

### Stress Tests
- [ ] Rapid sequential operations (10+ operations in quick succession)
- [ ] Concurrent operations from multiple client instances
- [ ] Long-running connection (maintain connection for 5+ minutes)
- [ ] Operations while CNC is running a program

### Error Handling Tests
- [ ] Connection timeout
- [ ] Invalid credentials
- [ ] Non-existent file download
- [ ] Permission errors
- [ ] CNC offline/unreachable
- [ ] CNC FTP server restart during operation

---

## Success Criteria

1. No CNC freezing or hanging during FTP operations
2. Successful connection reuse across multiple operations
3. Latency comparable to or better than working project
4. All existing API endpoints continue to work
5. Proper error handling and recovery
6. Clean connection cleanup (no resource leaks)

---

## Notes

- Passive mode is proven to work with Brother CNC from other project
- Active mode was implemented based on incorrect assumption in commit 423fff2
- Connection reuse pattern matches industry best practices for resource-constrained servers
- Brother CNCs typically support only 1-2 concurrent FTP connections
- Industrial equipment often has slower response times than modern servers (30s timeout appropriate)

---

## Risk Assessment

**Risk Level:** LOW

**Justification:**
- Passive mode is proven to work from other project
- Changes are isolated to FTP client implementation
- No API contract changes
- Easy rollback via git if issues occur
- Connection reuse is standard best practice

**Mitigation:**
- Implement in phases (passive mode first, then connection reuse)
- Test after each phase
- Keep working project as reference implementation
